 "result": "All of this is in `src/tessel/views.py`. `VerbView` subclasses `View`.\n\n1. **Declaring methods (`VerbView.__init_subclass__`, L165).**\n   - When the subclass is created, it collects `methods` from base classes plus any `http_method_funcs` names it defines (`get`, `post`, ...).\n   - The result is uppercased and stored as `cls.methods`, e.g. `{\"GET\", \"POST\"}`.\n\n2. **Making a view function (`View.to_view_func`, L86).**\n   - Builds a `view(**kwargs)` closure that instantiates the class (once per request if `init_every_request` is true, otherwise once up front) and calls `self.run_view(**kwargs)` through `active_app.ensure_sync`.\n   - Applies any `decorators`.\n   - Copies `view_class`, `__name__`, `__doc__`, `methods` and `provide_automatic_options` onto the function.\n   - The routing layer reads `view.methods`, so the rule is registered for those HTTP methods when you pass it to `attach_route_rule(..., view_func=...)`.\n\n3. **Dispatching (`VerbView.run_view`, L182).**\n   - Looks up `getattr(self, request.method.lower())`.\n   - A `HEAD` request with no `head` handler falls back to `get`.\n   - Calls the handler with the URL kwargs, again through `ensure_sync`.",
